          {
            "id": "63a8a4a38f48875a",
            "source_tier": "official",
            "channel": "nrl_news",
            "category": "Team Lists",
            "title": "NRL Late Mail: Round 21 - Panthers lose Edwards Presented by",
            "url": "https://www.nrl.com/news/2026/07/22/nrl-late-mail-round-21/",
            "published_at": "2026-07-23T01:54:20+00:00",
            "snippet": "A blow for the Panthers ahead of Thursday night's Battle of the West with gun fullback Dylan Edwards ruled out due to a head cut.\n\nEdwards suffered the gash during last week's loss to the Broncos that required 10 stitches.\n\nThe loss of David Fifita to suspension and Cameron Murra",
            "body_excerpt": "A blow for the Panthers ahead of Thursday night's Battle of the West with gun fullback Dylan Edwards ruled out due to a head cut.\n\nEdwards suffered the gash during last week's loss to the Broncos that required 10 stitches.\n\nThe loss of David Fifita to suspension and Cameron Murray and Tallis Duncan to injury has forced the Rabbitohs into a major reshuffle ahead of their crucial clash with the Storm.\n\nGoalkicking centre Latrell Siegwalt lines up for his career seventh game while Lachlan Hubner starts at lock and Liam Le Blanc is also set for a call-up.\n\nCowboys coach Todd Payten has recalled experienced playmaker Jake Clifford to partner Tom Dearden in the halves for a bumper showdown against the Broncos at a sold-out Queensland Country Bank Stadium.\n\nSee all the late mail, official team news and updates for Round 21 of the 2026 NRL Telstra Premiership competition.\n\nEels: Star playmaker Mitch Moses plays just his 13th game for the season as he returns from a corked thigh to take on Blues halves partner Nathan Cleary. Five-eighth Ronald Volkman suffered a head knock against the Roosters before the bye but has cleared the concussion protocols to take his place. Luca Moretti also returns from a concussion on the bench. No changes in Wednesday's update with Will Penisini remaining in the squad and a chance to return from a case of Osteitis Pubis that has sidelined him since Round 9.\n\nPanthers: Fullback Dylan Edwards has dropped out of the side as he continues his recovery from a head cut suffered last week and been replaced Thomas Jenkins. The shuffle sees Paul Alamoti push to the wing and Izack Tago come in at centre. Jaxen Edgar has been added to the bench. Edwards suffered a head cut that required 10 stitches post-match in last week's loss to the Broncos. Mitch Kenny (leg) could still be a couple of weeks away so Freddy Lussick will do the job as starting hooker for the 11th straight game. Winger Brian To'o needs one try to bring up a century of tries in the NRL.\n\nKnights: Veteran centre Dane Gagai has succumbed to calf tightness so the versatile Fletcher Hunt will start in the No.3 jersey.\u00a0Cody Hopwood returns from a calf injury on the bench while Sandon Smith is named in No.14 and will be hoping for game time this week after going unused against the Sharks. The Knights have won their last five games at McDonald Jones Stadium.\n\nRoosters: Skipper James Tedesco (concussion) is back on deck and centre Rob Toia returns after being given a post-Origin rest last ",
